/-!
# `Theta (C23) >= 11.334557922754518`, a deeper DAG on the coset port system

Writing `w` for the base realisation (exponent `1`),

```
n3   = Tt (w, w, w)              n9  = Tt (n3, n3, n3)      n27 = Tt (n9, n9, n9)
n54  = Aa (n27, n27)             n81 = Tt (n27, n27, n27)   n55 = Tt (n27, w, n27)
n190 = Uu (n54, n81, n55)
```

with the subscript of each node its strong-power exponent, and the `49`-word terminal code
`K` applied to `(n190, n190, n190, n190)`, giving exponent `4 * 190 = 760`.  The
base system lives in `C23^(box 4)`, so `M` is an independent set in `C23^(box 3040)`.

The bare exponent-`1` base appears as the middle child of `n55`, and the arity-`2`
substitution `Aa` occurs at `n54` within an otherwise arity-`3` layer.

-/

